  "paragraph": 18,
  "text": "The same hygiene applies to instructions and domain knowledge through progressive disclosure. Instead of stuffing twenty thousand tokens of repository guidelines, deployment checklists, and specialized docs into turn one, modern harnesses place a tiny static manifest in the prefix, just short names and one-line summaries. When the current task touches authentication, the harness loads the full auth skill file lazily into the appended message history, or invokes CLI tools via shell, keeping both the context window lean and the static prefix cache completely intact.",
